---
// X-home-act2 — OQ-1, resolved rather than deferred.
//
// THE QUESTION. The handoff's Home Act 2 is a 2x2 grid for four projects and
// omits Cairn entirely. D-38 locks five. UI-SPEC flagged this as having NO owner
// in Phase 0 despite Phase 0 being the design phase, and required the planner to
// do one of exactly two things: scope a single Act-2 sketch, or record an
// explicit Phase 5 deferral citing OQ-1. Leaving it implicit was named as the
// failure mode, because Phase 5 would then improvise a layout the handoff never
// specified, under build pressure, with no reviewer looking at it.
//
// THIS PLAN SCOPED THE SKETCH. One resolution, rendered, not a menu of options —
// a menu is a decision postponed with extra steps.
//
// THE RESOLUTION. The 2x2 is kept intact for the four projects the handoff
// actually drew, and the design system is promoted to a full-width row above it.
// Three reasons, in order of weight:
//   1. D-38 already names the design system the flagship, and gives a reason no
//      other project has: it is the only one whose outcome the reader is looking
//      at while reading about it. A layout that says so costs nothing extra.
//   2. It adds the fifth project without leaving a hole. A 2x3 grid with five
//      entries has an empty cell, and an empty cell in a 2x2-derived layout reads
//      as a missing project rather than as a composition.
//   3. It is the smallest possible change to an approved design. Every other
//      resolution — 3+2, a 5-column row, a scrolling strip — restyles Act 2
//      wholesale, and Act 2 is the one part of Home the handoff got signed off.
//
// SCOPE, DELIBERATELY NARROW. This sketch resolves the five-into-four problem
// and nothing else. Act 1, the name treatment and the peek gallery are PUB-01's
// in Phase 5 and are out of DSGN-03's scope; restyling them here would quietly
// annex Home into a phase that does not own it. The surrounding context is drawn
// in outline only, so the grid can be judged in place rather than in a vacuum.
//
// PLAN 00-22 MOVED ACT 2 INTO A COMPONENT AND CHANGED NOTHING ELSE HERE. The
// composition below is `../components/HomeAct2.astro`, and /home renders the
// same component. That is a refactor, not a redesign: the two routes could
// otherwise hold two copies of one APPROVED composition in the screenshot
// record, and two copies disagree the first time either is touched. The
// extraction was proved visually neutral rather than assumed — snap22.mjs
// compared every box's position, size, colour, font and text at all six device
// classes before and after, and the two snapshots are identical.
//
// Note that this artefact's Act 1 outline stayed here and is NOT what /home
// renders. /home builds the real state A — the name treatment, the six-photo
// peek grid and the scroll prompt, inside one viewport. The dashed outline below
// is this artefact's framing, kept so the grid can still be judged at the fold.

import { Eyebrow, Text } from "@akhil-saxena/design-system";
import Public from "../layouts/Public.astro";
import HomeAct2 from "../components/HomeAct2.astro";
import home from "../data/home_config.json";

const OCHRE_D_STRONG = "var(--ochre-d-strong)";
---

<Public title="X-home-act2 — OQ-1 resolved, five projects" active="home" maxWidth={1080}>
	<!--
	  Act 1 in outline only. Not designed here, not restyled here — /home is where
	  the real one lives, and PUB-01 owns it in Phase 5. It is drawn so the grid
	  below can be judged where it actually sits, at the fold, rather than
	  floating at the top of an empty page.
	-->
	<section class="ha-act1">
		<Eyebrow size="sm" tone="muted">ACT 1 — OUT OF SCOPE, PUB-01 / PHASE 5</Eyebrow>
		<div class="ha-act1-body">
			<div class="ha-act1-name">{home.title}</div>
			<div class="ha-act1-sub">{home.subtitle}</div>
			<div class="ha-act1-tag">{home.intro}</div>
			<div class="ha-act1-grid">
				{home.peekIds.map(() => <span class="ha-act1-tile" />)}
			</div>
			<Text size="sm" tone="muted" maxWidth={560}>
				The name treatment, the 3×2 peek gallery and its single stored
				<code>peekPosition</code> are Phase 5's. Outlined, not designed.
			</Text>
		</div>
	</section>

	<HomeAct2 />

	<Fragment slot="crosslink">
		<a class="ha-xlink" href="/work" style={{ color: OCHRE_D_STRONG }}>
			see the work →
		</a>
	</Fragment>
</Public>

<style>
	/* App LAYOUT css. Act 2's own geometry moved to components/HomeAct2.astro
	   with plan 00-22; what is left here is this artefact's framing. */

	.ha-act1 {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-3);
		padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
		opacity: 0.55;
	}

	.ha-act1-body {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-3);
		justify-items: center;
		text-align: center;
		border: 1px dashed var(--wire);
		border-radius: var(--radius-md);
		padding: var(--space-8);
	}

	.ha-act1-name {
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: var(--text-5xl);
		line-height: var(--lh-tight);
		letter-spacing: var(--ls-tighter);
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.ha-act1-sub {
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--ink-3);
	}

	.ha-act1-tag {
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--ink-2);
	}

	.ha-act1-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		/* The handoff's 14px is not on the 4px grid. Snapped to --space-4 (16px)
		   and the 2px delta recorded rather than introducing a 14px token — a 2px
		   gap delta on a 3x2 grid is below the threshold a reviewer can see. */
		gap: var(--space-4);
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 720px;
	}

	.ha-act1-tile {
		aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
		background: var(--cream-2);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.ha-xlink {
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
</style>
